Patches here apply on top of the kernel source snapshot.

0001 adds the NanoKVM PCIe board device tree (OLED and Wave420L nodes included)
and its dtb entry.  Board enablement is not part of the kernel source branch,
which only carries the SoC-level Wave420L controller node, its binding and the
driver; keeping the board out of that series lets the driver be reviewed and
submitted on its own.

0002 enables the CV1800B watchdog for that board, on top of the board file.

0003 advertises the C906's T-Head vector extension (RVV 0.7.1) on the SoC CPU
node, with the 128-bit vlenb the kernel's homogeneity check requires.  The
kernel would otherwise keep it disabled: the GhostWrite errata probe treats
every c9xx core (marchid/impid 0) as vulnerable and disables the extension, so
the board configuration turns CONFIG_ERRATA_THEAD_GHOSTWRITE off.  The C906 is
not affected by GhostWrite.

Camera, pinctrl, Ethernet, watchdog-node and Wave420L driver changes remain
kernel source commits in https://github.com/slopization/linux-cv181x-sodoport.
Do not duplicate those commits here.  The package remains 3.0 (quilt).
